<title>INDIA: India Britannia 1996/97 net higher.</title>
<headline>India Britannia 1996/97 net higher.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net Profit		179.0	vs     160.0</p>
<p>    Sales		   7,523.0	vs   6,024.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (in rupees)    4.0	vs	 4.0</p>
<p>    Profit before tax     295.0	vs     270.0</p>
<p>    Operating profit	233.0	vs     175.0</p>
<p>Note: Indian biscuit maker Britannia Industries Ltd did not give other details. The company said it spent about 386 million rupees on fixed assets and capital work-in-progress (including capital advances) as part of a restructuring programme.</p>
</text>
